(a) the year-wise and State-wise/UT-wise number of children reported missing since 2020-21 till date, including details of the number of traced and untraced children;
(b) the State-wise/UT-wise number of individuals arrested and convicted for child trafficking and the number of cases pending since 2020-21 till date; and
(c) the State-wise/UT-wise number of Anti-Human Trafficking Units (AHTUs) sanctioned, functional, along with details of the number of staff vacancies?

(a) the total storage capacity available with the Food Corporation of India (FCI), as on date, separately for Government owned godowns and privately hired/rented godowns;
(b) the  details of total storage capacity hired/rented or leased by the FCI since 2023-24, disaggregated by godowns, warehouses, silos and other storage facilities, year-wise and State/UT-wise;
(c) the details of payments made by FCI towards rented, leased or privately operated storage capacity since 2023-24, year-wise; and
(d) the details of private entities currently providing storage capacity to FCI, including capacity contracted and type of storage, company-wise?

(a) the State/UT-wise and year-wise details of LPG connections released under the Pradhan Mantri Ujjwala Yojana (PMUY) since 2021 and the number of active beneficiaries as on date;
(b) the State/UT-wise and year-wise details of PMUY beneficiaries who did not avail a single LPG refill since 2021; and
(c) the State/UT-wise and year-wise details of PMUY beneficiaries who availed less than three refills, three to six refills and more than six refills annually since 2021?

(a) the year-wise and zone-wise details of complaints received regarding quality of catered food in trains since 2023;
(b) the year-wise details of inspections conducted by Indian Railway Catering and Tourism Corporation (IRCTC) for trains with food catering services since 2023; and 
(c) the year-wise details of vendors and contractors fined, warned, suspended, blacklisted or issued show-cause notices for food quality and hygiene violations since 2023?

(a) the details of total outstanding liabilities/debt of Indian Railways for the last five years, indicating the amount owed under each source of borrowing, year-wise and source-wise;
(b) the details of interest incurred on borrowings of Indian Railways for the last five years, year-wise;
(c) the amount spent by Indian Railways on debt servicing for the last five years, separately indicating principal repayment and interest payment, year-wise; and
(d) whether the debt servicing burden of Indian Railways has increased as a share of its total capital expenditure and revenue expenditure, if so, the details thereof, year-wise?

(a) the State/UT-wise, year-wise and species-wise details of wildlife deaths linked to heat waves, heat stress, dehydration or water scarcity, since 2021;
(b) the State/UT-wise number of incidents of mass mortality or distress among wild animals and birds attributed to extreme heat conditions, since 2021;
(c) the measures taken to provide water sources, habitat management and emergency response mechanisms for wildlife during periods of extreme heat; and
(d) whether Government has formulated any national strategy to mitigate the impact of climate change and heat waves on wildlife and if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the year-wise details of funds mobilised for Bharatmala Pariyojana through budgetary support, borrowings, private participation and asset monetisation during last five years;
(b) the number and value of Bharatmala projects whose completion timelines have been revised beyond the originally scheduled date, indicating the average duration of delay; and
(c) the year-wise and State-wise/UT-wise details of delays and cost escalation under Bharatmala Pariyojana attributable to land acquisition, environmental clearances, utility shifting and other implementation constraints?

(a) the year-wise and source-wise share of renewable energy in the country’s total energy supply mix from 2021-22 till date;
(b) whether renewable energy’s share in the country’s total primary energy supply remains low despite growth in installed capacity, if so, the reasons thereof;
(c) what measures Government is taking to bridge this gap; and
(d) the year-wise and source-wise share of renewable energy in the country’s electricity generation from 2021-22 till date, along with the quantum of electricity generated from each renewable source?

(a) the year-wise targets set and achieved for household rooftop solar installations under the Pradhan Mantri Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana (PMSGMBY) since its launch;
(b) the State/UT-wise total number of households with solarised rooftops under the PMSGMBY, categorised by rooftop solar capacity, i.e. 1-2 kW, 2-3 kW and 3 kW and above; and
(c) the State/UT-wise total number of loan applications, sanctioned and disbursed for rooftop solar installations under the scheme, categorised by capacity, i.e. 1-2 kW, 2-3 kW and 3 kW and above, along with the total loan amount sanctioned and disbursed in each category till date?

(a) the breakup of mineral blocks offered for auction under 7th tranche of auction of critical and strategic minerals, including the types of critical and strategic minerals offered State/UT-wise and tranche-wise;
(b) the number of blocks offered as Mining Leases and Composite Licences under the latest auction;
(c) the total number of bids received for each critical mineral mine in the 7th tranche of auctions; and
(d) the details of tenders awarded to winning bidders for each critical mineral mine under the 7th round of auctions, including the name of the company, bid amount, proposed production capacity and timeline for commencement of operations?

(a) year-wise contribution of textile and apparel industry to India’s GDP since Financial Year 2021-22, and share of handloom, handicrafts and carpets sector in it;
(b) State/UT-wise registered handloom weavers, active loom households and weaver households that exited the sector during the last five years; 
(c) whether Government proposes to extend Employees’ State Insurance (ESI), Employees’ Provident Fund (EPF) and Employees’Pension Scheme (EPS) coverage to handloom weavers and allied workers, if so, details and timeline thereof; and
(d) whether over half of handloom units in Assam, Tamil Nadu and Uttar Pradesh has witnessed a decline in production, if so, the corrective measures proposed?

bs

(a) the State/UT-wise premium collected, claims received, claims approved, claims paid and claims pending under the Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY) since 2022;
(b) the State/UT-wise and year-wise details of private-sector insurance companies participating in the PMFBY since 2021;
(c) the details of year-wise premium collected by private and public sector insurance companies and claims paid to farmers between 2021-22 and 2025-26; and
(d) the insurer-wise details of claims pending beyond the prescribed timeline along with the value of such claims?

(a) the year-wise average real wages of workers in the rural and urban areas since 2021, including the categories of regular salaried employees, casual labourers and self-employed workers;
(b) whether Government has undertaken any assessment of the impact of stagnant real wages on domestic consumption and the standard of living in the country and if so, the details thereof; and
(c) the measures taken or proposed by Government to improve wage growth, quality of employment and income security for workers in both the organised and unorganised sectors?

(a) the State/UT-wise Central and District libraries set up, modernised or proposed under the National Mission on Libraries (NML) since inception;
(b) the year-wise budget allocated, funds released and expenditure incurred under the Mission;
(c) the State/UT-wise sanctioned posts, working strength and vacancies of librarians and staff;
(d) the State/UT-wise number of libraries digitised or under digitisation, including of manuscripts and books; and
(e) whether infrastructure gaps, staff shortages and digital access have been assessed and if so, the corrective measures taken thereon?

(a) the year-wise and State-wise/UT-wise number of candidates trained and placed under Artificial Intelligence and other emerging technology-related skilling programmes since 2019;
(b) whether Government has conducted any assessment regarding the gap between industry demand and employability of candidates trained under Skill India initiatives, if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor; and
(c) the details of measures taken to reduce the employability gap of candidates trained under Skill India initiatives?

(a) the details of the total number of digital payment frauds reported, category-wise, along with the total amount of money involved between 2021 and 2025, year-wise;
(b) the details of the amount recovered and returned to victims in such frauds during the same period, year-wise;
(c) whether Government has conducted any assessment regarding the rise in digital payment frauds  and  the vulnerability of senior citizens;
(d) if so, the measures being taken or being considered to address the crisis; and
(e) the details of budget allocation and expenditure incurred on cyber fraud awareness, year-wise and activity-wise?

(a) the number of internship opportunities announced, applications received, candidates selected and internships completed under the Prime Minister Internship Scheme (PMIS) since its inception month-wise and State/UT-wise;
(b) the details of internship positions offered and filled under the Scheme company-wise;
(c) whether Government maintains data on employment outcomes of interns after completion of internship and if so, the number of interns who secured jobs or continued employment, social category-wise;
(d) the details of budget allocation, funds released and actual expenditure incurred under PMIS since inception year-wise; and
(e) whether Government has conducted any review regarding implementation gaps, low participation or drop-out rates under the Scheme?

(a) total installed and operational coal gasification capacity in the country since 2019-20, plant-wise and year-wise; 
(b) coal requirement for coal gasification and for chemical plants since 2019-20, plant-wise and year-wise;
(c) product-wise current production from coal gasification and coal to chemical plants in the country, including synthetic gas, methane, synthetic natural gas, methanol, ammonia, ammonium nitrate, urea and other chemicals; 
(d) targets fixed and realised under the Coal Gasification Mission to achieve gasification of 100 million tonnes of coal by 2030 since 2021-22, year-wise; and
(e) details of coal gasification projects currently under construction, tendered, awarded or proposed and expected date of Commissioning?

(a) the details of Aviation Turbine Fuel (ATF) year-wise and category-wise since 2021;
(b) the year-wise details of increase in average airfares attributable to higher ATF prices and additional operating costs arising from airspace restrictions and route diversions since March, 2025 till date;
(c) whether Government has assessed the impact of rising domestic airfares on passenger traffic and regional connectivity; and
(d) the measures being taken to reduce operating costs and contain fare increases?

(a) the State/UT-wise details of funds released, utilised and remaining unspent  under the Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana (PMGSY) since Financial Year 2020-21;
(b) the State/UT-wise total number of PMGSY projects pending completion, along with their original date of sanction, original completion deadline and present stage of completion;
(c) the State/UT-wise details of delayed PMGSY projects which have reported cost escalation, including the original sanctioned cost, revised estimated cost and total cost overrun; and
(d) details of PMGSY projects terminated since Financial Year 2020-21, the State/UT-wise and year-wise alongwith the cost escalation due to such cancellations for each project?

(a) the sector-wise projected gains and losses for India under the EU- India FTA,  including employment  impact  in textiles,  automobiles, chemicals, pharmaceuticals, food processing, IT services and MSMEs;
(b) whether India has secured any exemption, waiver, or compensatory mechanism from the EU’s Carbon Border Adjustment Mechanism (CBAM), if not, the estimated cost  to  Indian  exporters  for  steel,  aluminium,  cement,  fertilisers and other downstream products, sector-wise; and
(c) whether the reported EU commitment of Euro 500 million for green transition is adequate against the estimated decarbonisation requirement of Indian heavy industry, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the current status of Rules under the Sustainable Harnessing and Advancement of Nuclear Energy for Transforming India (SHANTI) Act, 2025;
(b) the timeline by which Government proposes to notify the Rules;
(c) whether consultations have been held with stakeholders regarding the Rules and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) whether the proposed liberalisation of India’s nuclear sector under the SHANTI Act has been discussed or linked to any bilateral trade, investment, strategic, or technology negotiations with foreign Governments and if so, the details thereof, including the countries involved and nature of discussions?

(a) the details of budgetary allocations made and utilised under the North East Enterprise Development Scheme (NEEDS) since its inception, year-wise;
(b) the number of enterprises and projects financed through NEEDS in each State of the North Eastern Region, sector-wise and year-wise;
(c) whether Government has laid down implementation milestones or progress indicators to evaluate the impact of NEEDS and if so, the status of those benchmarks during 2025-26; and
(d) whether any independent review or audit has been undertaken to assess the effectiveness of NEEDS in catalysing entrepreneurship, job creation and sustainable development in the region and if so, the key findings thereof?

(a) the number of spam call complaints received during the last three years, State/UT-wise;
(b) the State/UT-wise number of telecom resources disconnected under the new TRAI framework, month-wise since its inception;
(c) whether Government is taking action on AI-flagged suspected spam without formal complaints;
(d) if so, the operating thresholds, safeguards against false positives and appeal mechanisms for wrongly impacted subscribers; and
(e) whether Government is considering placing the outcome metrics (spam reduction, fraud prevention, wrongful blocks) in the public domain to ensure transparency?

(a) the Budget allocation and actual expenditure of the Geological Survey of India (GSI) during the last five financial years, year-wise;
(b) whether Government has taken cognizance of observations of the Department-related Parliamentary Standing Committee regarding financial constraints in GSI;
(c) whether any projects relating to critical and strategic minerals have been delayed or deferred due to financial or manpower constraints; and
(d) the steps taken or proposed to augment financial allocation and technical capacity of GSI to meet the increased exploration requirements, particularly for critical minerals?

P

(a) the purpose-wise break-up of the ? 30,000 crore allocated for Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Act (MGNREGA) in the Union Budget 2026-27;
(b) State/UT-wise normative allocations budgeted under Viksit Bharat Guarantee for Rozgar and Ajeevika Mission Gramin (VB-GRAM-G) for Financial Year 2026–27, against the total outlay of ? 95,692 crore, along with the criteria used for determining such normative allocations;
(c) the status of roll-out of VB-GRAM-G and the stage-wise timeline for its implementation; and
(d) whether works proposed under Viksit Gram Panchayat Plans under VB-GRAM-G are required to be drawn exclusively from PM Gati Shakti?

(a) whether Government is considering a ban on social media for children, if so, the details thereof, if not, the reasons therefor;
(b) whether the Ministry has held any consultation with experts and stakeholders across other Ministries to develop frameworks for children’s online safety, if so, details thereof;
(c) whether the Ministry is exploring collaborations with the Ministry of Education to address rising digital addiction among children, if so, details thereof, if not, the reasons therefor; and
(d) the year-wise and State-wise/UT-wise number of child suicides recorded due to digital addiction since 2020?

(a) the year-wise, State-wise/UT-wise and component-wise details of the number of applications received, approved and rejected under the Scheme for Economic Empowerment of De-notified, Nomadic and Semi-Nomadic Tribes (SEED) during last five years;
(b) the year-wise details of the total budget allocated, funds released and funds utilised under the SEED scheme during last five years; and
(c) whether Government has identified De-notified (DNT), Nomadic (NT) and Semi-Nomadic communities (SNT) that are not included in any of the Scheduled Castes, Scheduled Tribes or Other Backward Classes lists and if so, the details thereof, including the number of such communities and their State-wise distribution?

(a) the year-wise details of the budget estimates and actual expenditure for the Pradhan Mantri Matsya Sampada Yojana (PMMSY) since Financial Year 2021-22;
(b) reasons for the reduction in PMMSY allocation from BE ? 2,465 crore to RE ? 1,500 crore in Financial Year 2025-26, along with major components where cuts were made;
(c) the year-wise quantity and amount of fisheries export since Financial Year 2021-22 till date and whether programme was successful in achieving its target of increasing fisheries export earnings to ? 1 lakh crore by 2024-25; and
(d) the year-wise and State-wise/UT-wise number of fishers covered under PMMSY fisher insurance since Financial Year 2021-22?

(a) the total number of reported fraud cases on the Unified Payments Interface (UPI) platform since 2022, with the total value of losses to users and the categories of fraud involved, year-wise;
(b) the steps taken since 2022 to strengthen fraud detection and prevention mechanisms on UPI, including safeguards adopted by the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) and National Payments Corporation of India (NPCI);
(c) the timeline of policy actions or guideline changes planned after the High Court notice dated February 2026 on UPI fraud safeguards; and
(d) the rationale for fixing the proposed digital payment fraud compensation limit by RBI?

(a) whether it is a fact that large number of litigation cases involving oil PSUs are pending for more than 10 years at various legal forums;
(b) whether Government has assessed the financial implications of such prolonged litigation;
(c) whether Government is considering to implement any monitoring mechanisms including online systems to reduce litigations; and
(d) if so, the details thereof, if not, the details therefor?

(a) State-wise break-up of the number of beneficiaries targeted and number trained under the Skilling (Traditional and Non-Traditional) component of the Pradhan Mantri Virasat Ka Samvardhan (PM VIKAS) scheme;
(b) State-wise break-up of the number of women beneficiaries targeted and number trained under the Leadership & Entrepreneurship (including Biz Sakhis) component of the scheme;
(c) State-wise break-up of the number beneficiaries enrolled in the Education Support (NIOS/bridge programmes) component of the scheme; and
(d) whether Government maintains data on the employment outcomes of beneficiaries trained under PM VIKAS, if so, the details thereof, component-wise?

(a) the total number of farmers covered and total area insured under the Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY), separately for Kharif and Rabi seasons during the last five years, year-wise;
(b) the total premium paid by farmers and total claims paid out by insurance companies under PMFBY, separately for Kharif and Rabi crops during the last five years, year-wise;
(c) the list of States currently not implementing the programme;
(d) the public sector and private insurance companies engaged for implementing PMFBY since 2021-2022, year-wise; and
(e) the claims paid by each participating insurance company under PMFBY since 2021-2022, year-wise?

(a) the number of manuscripts surveyed, catalogued and digitised under the Gyan Bharatam Mission since 2023, State-wise and language-wise;
(b) the funds sanctioned, released and utilised under the Mission since then, including on digitisation, conservation and digital repository development, year-wise and component-wise;
(c) the number of digitised manuscripts currently accessible to the public through official portals as on date and whether such access is free; and
(d) the  details of academic institutions, private collectors and research organisations working on the digitisation and dissemination of manuscripts, State-wise?

(a) whether Government acknowledges that Gram Urja Swaraj is presently a campaign without a dedicated scheme or budgetary allocation;
(b) whether any proposal for a stand-alone Centrally Sponsored Scheme for Gram Urja Swaraj has been prepared since the Standing Committee’s recommendation, if so, details thereof and if not, reasons therefor; and
(c) whether the Ministry has examined the Standing Committee’s recommendation to create a Rural Renewable Energy Fund under its own budget, if so, details thereof and if not, reasons therefor?

(a) the rank-wise details of the present sanctioned strength of the National Disaster Response Force (NDRF) and the number of vacancies therein;
(b) the location details of Regional Response Centres and Tactical Pre-Positioning Locations, along with the rank-wise sanctioned and posted strength at each such location;
(c) whether, in light of the increase in frequency and intensity of disasters, Government proposes to strengthen NDRF capacity by raising additional battalions, if so, details thereof; and
(d) the year-wise and State-wise details of volunteers trained, certified and currently ready for deployment under the Aapda Mitra Scheme?

(a) the number of recognised higher education institutions registered and live on the National Academic Depository (NAD) as on date, State-wise/UT-wise along with the number of academic records lodged and verified during each year since 2023;
(b) the number of disputes, complaints, verifications rejected or corrections recorded since 2023, category-wise;
(c) the details of protection and cyber security measures currently in place to safeguard student records and personal data;
(d) the timeline for full coverage of all recognised higher education institutions; and
(e) whether the Ministry proposes to publish annual usage and grievance metrics on a public dashboard and if so, details thereof?

(a) the details of the number of Nipah virus infections and deaths recorded in India over the past five years, year-wise and State/UT-wise;
(b) the measures Government is taking to contain the outbreak of Nipah across the country;
(c) whether Government is developing any contingency plans in case of nation-wide outbreak of Nipah virus, if so, the details thereof, if not, the reasons therefor;
(d) whether any reasons have been identified for the sudden and frequent outbreaks of Nipah virus in the country over the past few years; and
(e) whether Government has considered constituting a National Taskforce to address the increase in outbreaks?

(a) the total expenditure incurred on the Data Mining System (DMS) for the Corporate Data Management system (CDM) since Financial Year 2022-23, including vendor-wise payments for software licences and IT products;
(b) the year-wise number of instances in which analytics generated through the DMS under the CDM programme were shared with Registrars of Companies or Regional Directorates for scrutiny, inspection, inquiry or investigation; and
(c) the year-wise number of inspection, inquiry and investigation actions initiated where DMS analytics was a trigger and the outcomes, including prosecutions and compounding?

(a) the details of the quantity and value of bitumen imported into the country since 2015-16, along with the country-wise sources of such imports year-wise;
(b) the details of domestic production and total domestic consumption of bitumen during the same period and the percentage share of imports in total domestic consumption year-wise; and
(c) whether Government has assessed the adequacy of domestic bitumen production capacity in meeting the demand arising from national highway and infrastructure development programmes and if so, the details thereof?

(a) year-wise data since 2021 on the number of villages in the Union Territory of Ladakh reporting drinking water shortages and irrigation stress, along with estimated annual water deficit in cubic metres;
(b) the status of glacial retreat assessments for Ladakh’s river basins conducted by Government including year-wise data since 2021 on glacial area loss, change in snow cover and spring discharge levels;
(c) the projected water availability for Ladakh used in official planning documents for 2025 and 2030; and
(d) the funds allocated and utilised for water conservation and recharge measures in Ladakh since 2022?

(a) the year-wise total volume of domestic coal production and country-wise imports during the last five years, disaggregated by grade, along with data on pithead stockpiles held by Coal India Limited (CIL) and its subsidiaries as of January, 2026;
(b) the average cost incurred by CIL and other public sector coal companies on transporting coal to thermal power plants during this period and the estimated losses or underutilisation due to unsold pithead coal; and
(c) the details of power plants that continue to rely on imported coal in the country and reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government is aware that the Indian Broadcasting and Digital Foundation (IBDF) has urged Prassar Bharati to be more transparent in its e-auction of slots on the free Direct-To-Home (DTH) Doordarshan Free Dish platform;
(b) the State-wise list of participants affected by uncertain and unfair competition in the e-auction;
(c) whether the recommendations provided by the IBDF are being followed by Prasar Bharati; and
(d) the accountability guarantee that ensures that Prasar Bharati will provide a full disclosure to carry out a transparent bidding?

(a) the criteria used to restrict Minimum Support Price (MSP) coverage to 23 crops, despite over 200 crops being traded on the e-NAM platform;
(b) whether any crops have been formally considered and rejected for MSP coverage during the last five years, if so, the reasons therefor;
(c) the total value of fiscal transfers made directly to households in rural and urban areas during financial year 2024 and financial year 2025, State-wise, scheme-wise; and
(d) the percentage of farmers who have sold their produce at MSP during the last three agricultural years, State-wise?

(a) the number of instances across scientific institutions where funds remained blocked for more than three years due to non-enforcement of contractual penalties;
(b) the number of scientific equipments or prototypes procured during the last five years that remain unutilised or idle and the cumulative value of such idle assets; and
(c) the details of meteorological charges and statutory levies not realised due to absence of MoUs or agreements and whether recovery proceedings have since been initiated?

(a) steps taken to address disruptions in shipments, supply chains and the growing financial stress faced by fishers, seafood and dairy exporters and allied workers as a result of US tariffs;
(b) whether Government has conducted any consultation regarding the proposed India-US trade deal and its potential implications for the fisheries and dairy sectors;
(c) whether Government plans to open India’s domestic market to US-origin dairy and seafood products under the trade agreement; and
(d) if so, what measures are being considered to protect the livelihoods of small-scale dairy producers and traditional fishing communities?

(a) the actual market size of the Indian chemicals and petrochemicals sector as on end of 2025 and whether the projected target of $300 billion by 2025 has been achieved;
(b) the extent of growth in demand and production capacity recorded during the period leading up to 2025, vis-a-vis earlier projections;
(c) whether the target has not been achieved, if so, the reasons therefor, including constraints related to investments, infrastructure, policy implementation or global market conditions; and
(d) the roadmap and policy measures being pursued to achieve the long-term target of $1 trillion by 2040?

(a) whether Government is aware that under the Cinematograph (Certification) Rules 2024, the Board of Film Certification must meet once every quarter, where the last board meeting was held six years ago in August, 2019;
(b) whether Government is aware that the last annual report on the Central Board of Film Certification (CBFC) website dates back to 2016-17 and according to the rules, the board is required to publish and submit an annual report to the Ministry; and
(c) whether Government is aware that the CBFC was last reconstituted in 2017 for a period of three years until further order, which ended in 2020?

(a) the total value of Micro, Small, and Medium Enterprises (MSME) exports in financial year 2025-26, sector- wise and the sectors that registered the highest and lowest export growth in the past five years;
(b) details of financial and logistical support extended to MSMEs for export promotion, including the number of beneficiaries under various Government schemes, year-wise since 2015;
(c) details of any bilateral or multilateral collaborations initiated or being discussed with global trade bodies or partner countries to enhance MSME exports; and
(d) whether Government has assessed the impact of rising global protectionism and tariff barriers on India’s MSME exporters?

(a) whether Government has conducted any assessment of over tourism in India’s key tourist destinations;
(b) if so, the findings regarding peak tourist load, infrastructure stress and ecological degradation, State/UT-wise;
(c) whether it is a fact that several major tourist destinations face severe water shortages, waste accumulation, traffic collapse and increasing local resentment during peak tourist season; and
(d) the steps taken by Government to establish a national framework for sustainable tourism in the country?

(a) the basis on which the estimated number of unelectrified households was revised downward during SAUBHAGYA implementation;
(b) State-wise number of households currently identified as de-electrified or non-functional connections;
(c) the amount of extra-budgetary borrowings raised by Rural Electrification Corporation (REC) under SAUBHAGYA and related schemes; and
(d) the interest burden incurred on unutilised funds?

(a) the number of postfacto or retrospective environmental clearances granted since 2021, year-wise and State/UT-wise;
(b) the details of penalties collected from such cases, if any;
(c) the year-wise and State/UT-wise details of projects granted clearance despite being flagged by the Ministry’s own Expert Appraisal Committees;
(d) whether Government has conducted any assessment of ecological and economic consequences of regularising such projects; and
(e) if so, the findings thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the outstanding balances for all ongoing North-East Special Infrastructure Development Scheme (NESIDS) projects as on 31 December 2025, State-wise and sector-wise;
(b) the identified  projects where more than 50 per cent of approved cost remains unspent despite receiving sanctions more than two years ago;
(c) the number of projects that are currently delayed beyond the original completion timeline, State-wise; and
(d) the details of sectoral allocation since its inception, year-wise?

(a) the State-wise shortfall between Budget Estimates, Revised Estimates and Actual Expenditure under Pradhan Mantri Matsya Sampada Yojana (PMMSY) during the last three financial years;
(b) the number of States that failed to comply with SNA-SPARSH guidelines, year-wise and the specific nature of non-compliance;
(c) the State-wise allocation versus actual expenditure under the Scheduled Castes Sub-Plan (SCSP) component of PMMSY from 2022-23 to 2024-25; and
(d) the number of States that failed to submit proposals under SCSP during this period?

(a) the number of Government schools with functional computer labs and internet connectivity, along with the total number of Government school, State-wise/UT-wise;
(b) Government schools offering AI or digital literacy in their curriculum;
(c) whether national guidelines or pedagogical standards exist for AI education at the school level, if so, details thereof and if not, reasons therefor;
(d) the  number of Government school teachers trained in AI-related instruction and whether such training includes subject-specific capacity building, State-wise/UT-wise;
(e) whether learning outcome assessments have been conducted to evaluate these programmes; and
(f) the steps taken to prevent widening of digital divides due to disparities in infrastructure and teacher training?

(a) the number of education loan applications received, sanctioned, rejected and withdrawn, bank-wise and State-wise, during the last three financial years;
(b) whether Government has analysed the reasons for the significant gap between loan sanctions and actual disbursements under PM-Vidyalaxmi, if so, details thereof;
(c) the number of complaints received regarding illegal collateral or third-party guarantee demands for loans below the collateral-free threshold, State-wise;
(d) the number of higher-education institutions formally empanelled or linked with banks for education loan facilitation; and
(e) whether institutions in Tier-II and Tier-III cities show lower facilitation rates, if so, details thereof?

(a) the total value of loans written off by Public Sector Banks (PSBs) from Financial Year 2021-22 to Financial Year 2025-26, with PSB- wise and year-wise breakup for the last five years;
(b) the details of top 50 largest corporate accounts written off by PSBs during this period, bank-wise; and
(c) the value of loans written off and waived specifically for farmers in the same period, PSB-wise and year-wise?

(a) whether Government has taken note of reports regarding illegal massage centres and spas operating under the guise of Ayurvedic or Ayush clinics, including instances involving immoral trafficking;
(b) whether any licensing, inspection or monitoring mechanism exists to verify the authenticity of such establishments using Ayush nomenclature, if so, the number of registrations cancelled or suspended in the last three years;
(c) whether the Ministry coordinates with State Governments and law-enforcement agencies to prevent misuse of Ayush systems for illegal activities; and
